{"count": 579, "results": [{"id": "65aed98ce1f21415ea6f7ebd", "name": "LuckyMouse (APT27 or EmissaryPanda) | AVANGER X Bypass.exe", "description": "LuckyMouse (APT27 or EmissaryPanda) is a sophisticated cyber espionage group that has been active since at least 2010. | MSIL/Tedy.1448!tr is classified as a trojan. \nA trojan malware that performs activites without the user\u2019s knowledge. These activities commonly include establishing remote access connections, capturing keyboard input, collecting system information, downloading/uploading files, dropping other malware into the infected system, performing denial-of-service (DoS) attacks, and running/terminating processes.\nAkira Ransomware: Targeted Attacks, Data Breaches.\nAttacks Androids. Packed.", "author_name": "OctoSeek", "modified": "2024-02-21T21:04:46.152000", "created": "2024-01-22T21:09:32.433000", "tags": [], "references": [], "public": 1, "adversary": "LuckyMouse (APT27 or EmissaryPanda)", "targeted_countries": [], "malware_families": [], "attack_ids": [], "industries": [], "TLP": "white", "revision": 1, "groups": [], "in_group": false, "author": {"username": "OctoSeek", "id": "243548", "avatar_url": "/otxapi/users/avatar_image/media/avatars/user_243548/resized/80/avatar_3b9c358f36.png", "is_subscribed": false, "is_following": false}, "is_subscribing": null}, {"id": "65d065deda59dc1fc76e1cef", "name": "Cisco Anyconnect Vulnerability Analysis - Akira Ransomware - Truesec", "description": "The Akira ransomware group is likely to be actively exploiting an old Cisco Anyconnect vulnerability tracked as CVE-2020-3259, according to an analysis by the Truesec CSIRT team and a forensic analysis of recent incident response missions.", "author_name": "markusla", "modified": "2024-02-17T07:53:02.962000", "created": "2024-02-17T07:53:02.962000", "tags": [], "references": [], "public": 1, "adversary": "Akira", "targeted_countries": [], "malware_families": [], "attack_ids": [], "industries": [], "TLP": "white", "revision": 1, "groups": [], "in_group": false, "author": {"username": "markusla", "id": "251883", "avatar_url": "https://otx.alienvault.com/assets/images/default-avatar.png", "is_subscribed": false, "is_following": false}, "is_subscribing": null}, {"id": "658c45ad9b174d9cf1b26ce0", "name": "Akira, again: The ransomware that keeps on taking", "description": "The Sophos MDR Threat Intelligence team previously published the blog Akira Ransomware is \u201cbringin\u2019 1988 back\u201d in May 2023, roughly two months after the group was reported to have begun operations.", "author_name": "AlienVault", "modified": "2024-01-26T15:00:29.930000", "created": "2023-12-27T15:41:32.757000", "tags": [], "references": [], "public": 1, "adversary": "Akira", "targeted_countries": [], "malware_families": [], "attack_ids": [], "industries": [], "TLP": "white", "revision": 1, "groups": [], "in_group": false, "author": {"username": "AlienVault", "id": "2", "avatar_url": "/otxapi/users/avatar_image/media/avatars/user_2/resized/80/avatar_dacfad0ca8.png", "is_subscribed": true, "is_following": false}, "is_subscribing": null}, {"id": "65b1eff3d480775f1acb7e6b", "name": "VTA - Kasseika Ransomware Deploys BYOVD Attacks, Abuses PsExec and Exploits Martini Driver", "description": "Kasseika joins Akira, BlackByte, and AvosLocker in using the tactic that allows threat actors to terminate antivirus processes and services for the deployment of ransomware. In this case, research found that the Kasseika ransomware abused Martini driver to terminate the victim machine\u2019s antivirus-related processes. \u202fIt utilized targeted phishing techniques for initial access, gathering credentials. It used remote administration tools (RATs) to gain privileged access and lateral movement. The ransomware also abused legitimate windows RAT PsExec to execute malicious files such as .bat file and utilize a batch script to load its malicious entities. Kasseika\u2019s KILLAV exploited the vulnerabilities of signed driver that has a legitimate and trusted certificate. The payload continuously scanned all active processes in the system and terminated at least 991 processes within its list, and that also includes antivirus products, security tools, analysis tools, and system utility tools.", "author_name": "Provintell-Lab", "modified": "2024-01-25T05:21:55.298000", "created": "2024-01-25T05:21:55.298000", "tags": [], "references": [], "public": 1, "adversary": "Kasseika", "targeted_countries": [], "malware_families": [], "attack_ids": [], "industries": [], "TLP": "white", "revision": 1, "groups": [], "in_group": false, "author": {"username": "Provintell-Lab", "id": "112104", "avatar_url": "https://otx.alienvault.com/assets/images/default-avatar.png", "is_subscribed": false, "is_following": false}, "is_subscribing": null}, {"id": "65b14dad54060636a7291eb0", "name": "Kasseika Ransomware Deploys BYOVD Attacks, Abuses PsExec and Exploits Martini Driver", "description": "Following an increase in bring-your-own-vulnerable-driver (BYOVD) attacks launched by ransomware groups in 2023, the Kasseika ransomware is among the latest groups to take part in the trend. Kasseika joins Akira, BlackByte, and AvosLocker in using the tactic that allows threat actors to terminate antivirus processes and services for the deployment of ransomware. In this case we investigated, the Kasseika ransomware abused Martini driver to terminate the victim machine\u2019s antivirus-related processes.", "author_name": "AlienVault", "modified": "2024-01-24T17:56:05.390000", "created": "2024-01-24T17:49:33.471000", "tags": [], "references": [], "public": 1, "adversary": "Kasseika", "targeted_countries": [], "malware_families": [], "attack_ids": [], "industries": [], "TLP": "white", "revision": 2, "groups": [], "in_group": false, "author": {"username": "AlienVault", "id": "2", "avatar_url": "/otxapi/users/avatar_image/media/avatars/user_2/resized/80/avatar_dacfad0ca8.png", "is_subscribed": true, "is_following": false}, "is_subscribing": null}, {"id": "65b097e7f804150d78f9f6bd", "name": "Kasseika Ransomware Deploys BYOVD Attacks, Abuses PsExec and Exploits Martini Driver", "description": "ollowing an increase in bring-your-own-vulnerable-driver (BYOVD) attacks launched by ransomware groups in 2023, the Kasseika ransomware is among the latest groups to take part in the trend. Kasseika joins Akira, BlackByte, and AvosLocker in using the tactic that allows threat actors to terminate antivirus processes and services for the deployment of ransomware. In this case we investigated, the Kasseika ransomware abused Martini driver to terminate the victim machine\u2019s antivirus-related processes. \u202f\n\nIn our analysis of the Kasseika ransomware attack chain, we observed indicators that resemble the BlackMatter ransomware. These indicators include pseudo-ransom extensions and the use of extension string.README.txt as the ransom note file name and format.", "author_name": "tr2222200", "modified": "2024-01-24T04:53:59.729000", "created": "2024-01-24T04:53:59.729000", "tags": [], "references": [], "public": 1, "adversary": "", "targeted_countries": [], "malware_families": [], "attack_ids": [], "industries": [], "TLP": "white", "revision": 1, "groups": [], "in_group": false, "author": {"username": "tr2222200", "id": "207905", "avatar_url": "https://otx.alienvault.com/assets/images/default-avatar.png", "is_subscribed": false, "is_following": false}, "is_subscribing": null}, {"id": "6586dc3143921526cbad43fd", "name": "Akira Ransomware Latest Iteration Analysis", "description": "", "author_name": "cryptocti", "modified": "2024-01-22T13:00:54.027000", "created": "2023-12-23T13:10:09.283000", "tags": [], "references": [], "public": 1, "adversary": "", "targeted_countries": [], "malware_families": [], "attack_ids": [], "industries": [], "TLP": "white", "revision": 1, "groups": [], "in_group": false, "author": {"username": "cryptocti", "id": "110256", "avatar_url": "/otxapi/users/avatar_image/media/avat